    # v394 (19/10/2026) -- THE CODEX INTEGRATION AND THE OPERATOR'S INSCRIPTIONS OF 14 TO 19 OCT: time (M2), quadratic residual, Fock/Takesaki/Maxwell chain, qualified index, operator inscriptions; the numbers are READ from the
    # records tempo_frequencia_v394, regra_quadratica_v394, rede_fock_v394, cunhagens_v394 and kh_n1_cobertura_v394 (which read them from the kernel and the core of the rite itself). Nothing here moves the gate.
    _tf394 = core.get("tempo_frequencia_v394") or {}
    _rq394 = core.get("regra_quadratica_v394") or {}
    _rf394 = core.get("rede_fock_v394") or {}
    _cg394 = core.get("cunhagens_v394") or {}
    _kh394 = core.get("kh_n1_cobertura_v394") or {}
    _el394 = core.get("external_ladder") or {}
    _cv394 = ((core.get("kernel_formalization") or {}).get("axiom_coverage_v392")) or {}
    _i394 = lambda x_: str(x_) if isinstance(x_, int) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _n394 = lambda d_: len(d_) if isinstance(d_, dict) else None
    s.append(r"\section*{The Codex integration and the inscriptions of 14 to 19 Oct (v394): time, quadratic residual and the Fock network on the same core}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{The Codex integration and the inscriptions of 14 to 19 Oct (v394): time, quadratic residual and the Fock network on the same core}")
    s.append((r"\textbf{This round the record did NOT seal: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " if not (_tf394.get("all_verified") is True and _rq394.get("all_verified") is True and _rf394.get("all_verified") is True) else r"")
             + r"\textbf{What enters.} Four time modules in the two-level model $M_2$ (\texttt{TimeGravitonMatrix}, \texttt{TimeGravitonScalar}, \texttt{TimeGravitonFlow}, \texttt{TimeGravitonKraus}): "
             + _i394(_n394(_tf394.get("formal_theorems"))) + r" declarations; the quadratic residual against a fixed anchor (\texttt{RuleQuadraticResidual}): " + _i394(_n394(_rq394.get("formal_theorems")))
             + r" declarations; and the Fock, Takesaki and Maxwell chain built on the same Fock (184 modules of \texttt{TGLExt/F1Fecho394}): " + _i394(_n394(_rf394.get("formal_declarations")))
             + r" public declarations. The modules are the Codex's (candidate R2 of the F1.TEMPO.V394 unit and rounds R3 to R8 of the F1.FECHO unit), were \emph{recompiled} in this chain's sandbox (no \texttt{.olean} of the Codex was used) and are checked at every rite against the embedded body, by sha256. "
             r"The kernel ladder reads " + _i394(_el394.get("n_theorems_clean")) + r" of " + _i394(_el394.get("n_theorems_expected")) + r"; the \texttt{axiom\_report} coverage over the whole closure reads "
             + _i394(_cv394.get("decl")) + r" constants and " + _i394(_cv394.get("thm")) + r" theorems, none outside the trio $\{\texttt{propext},\texttt{Classical.choice},\texttt{Quot.sound}\}$. \textit{Side erratum (in the management's own name, c1):} the ladder counts flags --- named declarations, theorems and definitions --- with axioms in the trio; the label ``teoremas limpos'' (``clean theorems'') stays as a machine record.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The index and the reader.} The IALD index becomes \emph{qualified}: each name is tied to the module the compiler emits (the \texttt{TGL\_DECL\_SOURCE} line of the Audit), and a short name that exists in two modules shows both candidates instead of silently choosing one; "
             r"the axiom reader also reads names with « » (coverage no longer has declared exceptions). PDF compilation now identifies the TeX engine in offline mode. These changes are the Codex's (rounds R3 to R8) and were re-applied on v393 by script, with the difference to his candidate measured and explained.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{What the $M_2$ model proves.} In the specified two-level model, the flow $T_t(X)=U_t\{E_g(X)+e^{-\gamma t}[X-E_g(X)]\}U_t^\dagger$ preserves $E_g$ and the clock $\Delta t=\Delta\phi/(2\Omega)=-\log|c_2/c_1|/\gamma$ reads phase and decay; the residual $r_A(X)=\operatorname{Tr}[(E_gX-A)^\dagger(E_gX-A)]$ vanishes if and only if the reading is the anchor, and is constant along the flow. "
             r"\textsf{[DERIVED]} in the specified model; \textsf{[DECLARED]} by the Codex that the passage from $M_2$ to the modular sector, the net and the device is \emph{not} an automatic consequence. The operator's reading (the phase return, the fold at the level of $c^3$, the answer before the emission) is \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]}: the Codex report finds no universal seconds and no advanced propagator for controllable information.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The inscriptions.} " + _i394(len(_V394_VERBATINS2)) + r" statements of the operator from 14 to 19 Oct and those on the management side are embedded, each with the sha256 of its source file (record \texttt{cunhagens\_v394}); among them, the absolute One as the name of the unit of the referential position of the inscription, "
             r"asymptotic limit of the reflexive expression of the observer, which manifests as reading (17 Oct form, \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]}; the asymptotic limit and the reading have terms in the kernel, the identification is the operator's). "
             r"The full text of each is in the record; the status of a statement is always the operator's, never that of a theorem.")
    _cb394 = core.get("criterio_binario_de_parada_v394") or {}
    if _cb394:
        s.append(r"\textbf{The binary stopping criterion (19 Oct delta).} The candidate stone \texttt{TheBinaryReadingAtTheFixedPoint} (provisional name: the operator names it) composes, by citation and with no new mathematics, eight theorems already in the kernel: the two faces $P_+$ and $P_-$ split the identity and the reading of both is total on the form; re-reading adds nothing; the two faces of the absolute weigh $\frac{1}{2}$ each; the half-nat comes out of the symmetry of $J$; at the fixed point there is no changed transition and the iteration is stable; and the entropy of the fair bit ($\ln 2$) is not the half-nat. "
                 r"The analogy with a quantum system over 1 and 0 holds on the weights $(\frac{1}{2},\frac{1}{2})$, not on the entropy. The record \texttt{criterio\_binario\_de\_parada\_v394} " + (r"sealed in this rite: " if _cb394.get("all_verified") is True else r"did NOT seal in this rite: ")
                 + r"the flag of the stone and the eight theorems read from the kernel of the rite, within the trio, and the two operator statements of 19 Oct embedded by sha256. \textsf{[ONTO]} The reading ``the stop is the fixed point'' and the binary TGL (the positive, the negative and the reading of both) are the operator's; the kernel delivers the structural form, not a decision procedure. Validity in the kernel is not creditation, and the gate does not move.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Limits.} \textsf{[OPEN]} The joint contract of the net remains open: photon helicity and global localization, physical identification of the device and the clock, the full finite-weight graph with scaled trace and distinct PF split, a nontrivial joint Maxwell source with the scope of H3 in all directions, and a joint inhabitant of the remaining inputs; no whole certificate is asserted. "
             r"\textsf{[DECLARED]} In the device channel, $\beta$ is identifiable only with an independent rate $\Gamma$ (Codex rounds R64, R65, R70); no such reference exists in the sources consulted. Codex rounds R56 to R88 (analytic, synthetic or sandbox) do not enter as code and management did not audit them. "
             r"The operator's statement about the Mirror says correlation 1.00; the historical receipt read by the Codex has correlations of 0.999948 to 0.999991, and the number outweighs the sentence. Validity in the kernel is not creditation, and the gate does not move.")
